nitrovin

Data: the vehicle data this decoder ships is NHTSA's vPIC (Vehicle Product
Information Catalog), published by the U.S. National Highway Traffic Safety
Administration at https://vpic.nhtsa.dot.gov/ as a work of the United States
Government. The decoding procedure this project ports, `spVinDecode`, is part
of that publication. Each release records the vPIC data month it was built
from. NHTSA's terms of use (https://www.nhtsa.gov/about-nhtsa/terms-use) say
the information "may be distributed or copied"; NHTSA does not endorse this
project.

Reference implementation: the port's structure, its parity method and its
registry of documented upstream defects follow ultravin
(https://github.com/blackthorn-interstellar/ultravin, MIT, Bryce Drennan).
No ultravin source is copied; where a design or an evidenced deviation is
adopted, the file that adopts it says so.

Corpus: the committed parity corpus includes the VINs of ultravin's
`tests/parity_corpus.json` and its cover set (MIT). Only the VINs are taken;
every answer in this repository is produced by NHTSA's procedure in Postgres.
The corpus file's header names the source file and commit.

htmx: the /ui pages load htmx (https://htmx.org, Zero-Clause BSD), vendored
unmodified as pkg/ui/static/htmx.min.js.

axe-core: TestForm audits the pages with axe-core
(https://github.com/dequelabs/axe-core, Mozilla Public License 2.0, Deque
Systems, Inc.), vendored unmodified, its license header intact, as
cmd/nitrovin/testdata/axe.min.js. It is test data: no binary or image ships
it.

Benchmarks: the README's benchmarks (docs/benchmarks.md) follow ultravin's
method (its docs/BENCHMARKS.md and scripts/bench/), and their corpus is made
by ultravin's own generator, run from an ultravin checkout. nitrovin's
harness (bench/decode, scripts/bench.sh) is written fresh; no corpus
is committed.
